491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1485 0 R
/E (Transformers. Attention-based sequence models [6] handle long histories. NVIDIA's Cosmos models use transformers inside both diffusion and autoregressive designs [7], and GAIA-1 treats driving as next-token prediction over video, text and action inputs [8].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1486 0 R
/E (Reinforcement learning \(RL\). An RL agent learns by trial and error. Model-based RL adds a learned model of the environment that the agent can plan with or train inside [9]. DreamerV3 and MuZero both belong here [4][5].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1487 0 R
/E (Generative models. Diffusion and autoregressive generators can produce rich future frames. Genie 3 creates interactive worlds frame by frame from a text prompt, responding to the user's actions in real time [10].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1488 0 R
/E (Latent representations. Predicting every pixel wastes effort on details nobody can predict, like the exact motion of leaves. Joint-embedding approaches such as JEPA predict in an abstract representation space instead [3], and V-JEPA 2 applies that idea to video at scale [11].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 178 0 R
/T (Real-World Applications)
/E (Real-World Applications)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1489 0 R
/E (Autonomous vehicles. GAIA-1 generates driving scenes from video, text and action inputs, with control over the ego vehicle's behaviour [8]. Waymo's 2026 World Model, built on Genie 3, generates camera and lidar data so engineers can ask in simulation what would have happened had the driver acted differently [12]. Waymo describes three ways to steer a simulation, through driving actions, scene layout and language, and says the model can turn ordinary dashcam video into a multi-sensor simulation [12].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1490 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1491 0 R
/E (Gaming and simulated worlds. DreamerV3 became the first algorithm to collect diamonds in Minecraft from scratch, with no human data or curricula [4]. Rewards in that game are sparse, so the agent has to search for trees, cross lakes and traverse mountains long before a diamond appears [4]. Genie 3's generated worlds have also been used to test DeepMind's SIMA agent [10].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1492 0 R
/E (Healthcare. Work here is early. A 2025 review, which calls itself the first focused survey of the area, covers imaging, disease progression from health records and robotic surgery, and notes that actions, validation and patient state are hard to specify [13]. It also proposes a capability rubric for judging such systems [13].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1493 0 R
/E (Scientific discovery. GraphCast is a learned weather simulator rather than an agent's world model, but the idea is the same: learn dynamics from data, then roll forward. It beat a leading operational system on 90% of 1,380 verification targets [14]. It was trained directly on historical reanalysis data, and its forecasts also improved the tracking of severe events such as tropical cyclones [14].)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
