509 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 179 0 R
/T (What they offer)
/E (What they offer)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1498 0 R
/E (Cheaper, safer practice. Agents can rehearse in imagination before acting. NVIDIA's Cosmos paper points out that exploratory actions in the real world can damage a system and its surroundings [7].)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1499 0 R
/E (Data efficiency. DreamerV3's larger models both scored higher and needed less interaction to solve tasks [4], and V-JEPA 2 reached robot planning with a small amount of robot data [11].)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1500 0 R
/E (What-if reasoning. Genie 3's promptable world events let users change the weather or add objects to test counterfactual situations [10].)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 179 0 R
/T (Where they still fall short)
/E (Where they still fall short)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1501 0 R
/E (Compounding errors. Generating a world frame by frame lets inaccuracies pile up over time [10], and a 2026 survey lists compounding prediction errors and sim-to-real transfer among the open problems [15].)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1502 0 R
/E (Short memory and narrow scope. Genie 3 stays consistent for a few minutes, with visual memory reaching back about a minute. DeepMind also lists a restricted range of agent actions and difficulty simulating several independent agents [10].)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1503 0 R
/E (Looks versus physics. Generative models can lack the physical grounding and temporal reasoning needed for high-stakes decisions such as clinical support [13].)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 179 0 R
/T (Abstract)
/E (Abstract)
