<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Three directions look most promising, and each comes with a caveat.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Autonomous systems. The nearest-term use is simulation. DeepMind expects worlds like Genie 3's to train robots and autonomous systems and to help evaluate agents and expose their weaknesses [10]. The longer-term goal, LeCun's vision of agents that plan by simulating outcomes [3], needs models that stay accurate far longer than today's few minutes.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Intelligent decision-making. If a model predicts consequences reliably, a planner can test many options before choosing one. In medicine and driving, the weak point is validation: until predictions are checked against real interventions [13] and compared fairly across systems [15], they should support human judgement rather than replace it.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 179 0 R
/T (Conclusion)
/E (Conclusion)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [18]
>>
