586 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 183 0 R
/T (Privacy and Data Sovereignty)
/E (Privacy and Data Sovereignty)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
587 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (If your company handles internal documents, patient files, legal agreements, or proprietary code, you could be subject to regulations like GDPR, HIPAA, and SOC 2 that restrict or prohibit use of third-party AI APIs. Local inference guarantees data sovereignty, and prompts and responses are never transmitted outside of the organization. That said, local inference doesn't imply a fully secured environment; the security classification is influenced by software stack, source of the model, network profile, and system setup.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 183 0 R
/T (7.2 Latency)
/E (7.2 Latency)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The Cloud AI would have to traverse a network, adding around 100-500ms before starting the inference. Local AI by definition reduces no such network hops. Removing the network latency would have a tangible impact on user experience for interactive use cases, like code completion, live writing aids and chatbots.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
590 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 183 0 R
/T (7.3 Offline Operation)
/E (7.3 Offline Operation)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (Local models can continue to run, even if isolated from the internet, once the model files can be located. You will be able to run LM Studio in an offline mode, complete with local document-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\). This feature makes local AI a must-have feature when offline access is unavoidable; field, airplane, secured sites, remote, etc.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (Running an LLM from the command line is technically possible but not practical for most users. Applications such as LM Studio and Ollama provide higher-level interfaces for managing and running local models.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
