622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (We haven't only been developing bigger models and more powerful data centers. We have also been developing an opposite trend: miniaturizing, optimizing, and enhancing the flexibility of AI models so they can run locally. Techniques such as GPTQ, AWQ, or mixed-precision k-quants can shrink models by factors of 4-16 with surprisingly little impact on quality. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The GGUF format provides a simple, extensible, portable container format for hosting quantized models. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (Inference engines such as llama.cpp make it easy to run these models on a wide range of off-the-shelf hardware thanks to multi-backend acceleration. And tools like LM Studio or Ollama take the technical complexity out of local model hosting, offering GUIs, model management, and API compatibility.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
